# Mobile Responsive — Desktop Freeze Rule

## Current Task Scope

We are **only fixing mobile responsiveness** for the HSRL dashboard.
The desktop view is **complete, approved, and must not change**.

## Hard Rules

1. **Never modify desktop layout classes** — any class that applies at `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:`, or `2xl:` breakpoints must be left exactly as-is.
2. **Only add or change classes at `sm:` and below** (default/base styles, `sm:` prefix).
3. **Do not restructure JSX** in a way that affects desktop rendering — only wrap, conditionally show, or reorder elements for mobile using `block sm:hidden` / `hidden sm:block` patterns.
4. **Do not touch grid columns, flex layouts, padding, margin, font sizes, or widths** that are expressed at `md:` or larger — these are desktop-only and are frozen.
5. **Do not change any component's props, state, or data-fetching logic** while fixing mobile — layout only.

## What You Can Touch

- Base (no prefix) Tailwind classes **only when they don't affect desktop** (i.e. overridden at `md:` or higher).
- Add new `sm:`-prefixed classes.
- Add mobile-only wrapper divs / flex containers that collapse at `md:`.
- Adjust `overflow`, `truncate`, `text-xs`, `px-2`, `py-1` etc. at base/`sm:` level.

## Pattern to Follow

```jsx
// GOOD — base style for mobile, md: restores desktop
<div className="flex flex-col gap-2 md:flex-row md:gap-4">

// GOOD — show only on mobile
<div className="block md:hidden">...</div>

// GOOD — show only on desktop (unchanged)
<div className="hidden md:block">...</div>

// BAD — changing a desktop breakpoint class
<div className="md:grid-cols-3">  ← DO NOT TOUCH if it was md:grid-cols-4
```

## Verification Checklist (before saving)

- [ ] Desktop (≥768px) renders identically to before the change
- [ ] No `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:`, `2xl:` classes were added, removed, or modified
- [ ] No JSX structure changes that could reorder desktop elements
- [ ] No prop/state/logic changes

## Scope

This rule applies to all files under `frontend/src/` for the duration of the mobile responsiveness work.
